# VADAR Video Analysis Extension — Implementation Plan

Extends VADAR from single-image visual reasoning to **video analysis** by unlocking SAM 2's built-in Video Predictor, adding temporal modules, and adapting the LLM prompt pipeline.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hardware**: SAM 2 Video Mode requires **≥16 GB VRAM** for comfortable use. A chunked processing fallback (50 frames at a time) will be implemented for lower-VRAM GPUs.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Scope**: This plan adds video as a **new mode** alongside the existing image mode. All existing image functionality remains untouched. The new code lives in new files or clearly separated sections.

> [!WARNING]
> **SAM 2 Video Predictor dependency**: The installed `sam2` library must include `sam2.sam2_video_predictor`. We'll verify this at import time and raise a clear error if unavailable.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Video Utilities

New helper functions for video I/O (frame extraction, JPEG output directory management, chunked processing).

#### [NEW] [video_utils.py](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/video_utils.py)

- `extract_frames(video_path, output_dir, fps=None)` — Extracts frames from a video file into a JPEG directory (required by SAM 2 Video Predictor). Supports limiting to `fps` frames per second.
- `get_video_metadata(video_path)` — Returns resolution, total frames, FPS, duration.
- `chunk_frame_indices(total_frames, chunk_size=50)` — Splits frame indices into chunks for low-VRAM processing.
- `frames_to_video(frame_dir, output_path, fps)` — Re-assembles annotated frames into an output video.

---

### Component 2: Video-Aware Predefined Modules

Extends [predefined_modules.py](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/predefined_modules.py) with video-specific module classes and a `VideoModulesList`.

#### [MODIFY] [predefined_modules.py](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/predefined_modules.py)

Add the following new classes (appended after existing code):

| Class | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `VideoTrackModule` | Uses `SAM2VideoPredictor` to track objects across frames. Takes an initial point/bbox + frame index, returns per-frame masks & bboxes. |
| `VideoLocateModule` | Runs [LocateModule](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/predefined_modules.py#56-214) on individual frames (sampling) to find objects that weren't in the initial frame. |
| `VideoVQAModule` | Runs VQA on a specific frame (delegates to existing `VQAModule.predict()`). |
| `VideoResultModule` | Aggregates temporal data (e.g., count events, compute displacement, average attribute). |
| `VideoModulesList` | Initializes SAM 2 in **video mode** (`SAM2VideoPredictor`) alongside GroundingDINO/Molmo. Manages memory with chunked processing. |

Key implementation details:

```python
from sam2.sam2_video_predictor import SAM2VideoPredictor

class VideoTrackModule(PredefinedModule):
    """Track an object across video frames using SAM2 Video Predictor.
    
    Usage: track(video_dir, frame_index, x, y) → dict of {frame_idx: bbox}
    """
    def __init__(self, sam2_video_predictor, device, chunk_size=50, trace_path=None):
        super().__init__("track", trace_path)
        self.predictor = sam2_video_predictor
        self.device = device
        self.chunk_size = chunk_size

    def execute(self, video_dir, init_frame_idx, x, y):
        """Initialize tracking from a point and propagate across all frames."""
        # 1. Initialize video state
        # 2. Add point prompt at init_frame_idx
        # 3. Propagate masks across frames (chunked if needed)
        # 4. Convert masks → bounding boxes per frame
        # Returns: {frame_idx: [x1, y1, x2, y2]}
```

