### Component 3: Video Engine

A new engine class that handles the video execution pipeline.

#### [NEW] [video_engine.py](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/video_engine.py)

- `VideoEngine` extends the execution model: instead of receiving a single [image](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/engine_utils.py#153-161), the LLM-generated program receives a `video_dir` (path to extracted JPEG frames), `frame_count`, `fps`, and the video module functions.
- Reuses the same [_add_program_to_file](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/engine.py#540-568) / [_execute_file](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/agents/agents.py#570-586) pattern from [Engine](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/engine.py#29-606).
- Provides `video_dir`, `frame_count`, `fps`, and module functions in the namespace.
- The LLM writes a Python script that loops over frames and calls tracking/locating/VQA as needed.

Key difference from [Engine](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/engine.py#29-606):

| Aspect | Image Engine | Video Engine |
|---|---|---|
| Input | Single [image](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/engine_utils.py#153-161) | `video_dir`, `frame_count`, `fps` |
| Namespace | [image](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/engine_utils.py#153-161), [loc](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/demo-notebook/notebook_imports.py#364-401), [vqa](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/demo-notebook/notebook_imports.py#443-457), [depth](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/demo-notebook/notebook_imports.py#403-419), etc. | `video_dir`, `frame_count`, `fps`, `track`, `loc_frame`, `vqa_frame`, `get_frame`, etc. |
| LLM code pattern | Direct calls on [image](file:///c:/Users/mahesh/Documents/Mahesh/AI/VADAR/engine/engine_utils.py#153-161) | Loops over frames, temporal logic |

